This package emits no C# codegen types: it is a Daml library of functions and
re-exports of types owned by other packages, so the C# codegen produces no .cs
output for it.

The presence of this marker tells DriftDetectionTests to pin the snapshot as
emitting zero .cs, and to fail if codegen ever produces a .cs — so a future
type-bearing change is caught rather than shipped unnoticed. The publish-time
guard reads the same marker before accepting an empty generated tree. See
README.md. If the package legitimately gains a codegen-visible type, remove this
marker and refresh the expected/ snapshot.
